{%- comment -%}
One icon per postType, from the Font Awesome sprite the social counts
(post-social-counts.liquid) already use. Shape was tried and rejected;
colour was tried and rejected (see _geometric.scss). An icon is legible
without decoding.

Split out of post-list-entry.liquid and captured by every one of that
partial's callers BEFORE the `page: post` override they apply, for the
identical reason post-social-counts.liquid's `socialHtml` already is:
@11ty/font-awesome files each {% icon %}'s sprite symbol against
`this.page.url` (plugin.js:51). Called from inside the override, the symbol
files under the POST's own url instead of the listing page's, so the
listing's {% getBundle %} never outputs it and the <use> it left behind
resolves to nothing — the icon renders blank. Capturing here, before the
override, files it against the real listing page.

Expects a local `post` (one collections.post item), passed by each of
post-list-entry.liquid's callers.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- case post.data.postType -%}
	{%- when "article" %}{% icon "far:file-lines" %}
	{%- when "bookmark" %}{% icon "far:bookmark" %}
	{%- when "like" %}{% icon "far:heart" %}
	{%- when "photo" %}{% icon "far:image" %}
	{%- when "reply" %}{% icon "fas:reply" %}
	{%- when "audio" %}{% icon "fas:music" %}
	{%- when "video" %}{% icon "fas:video" %}
	{%- when "event" %}{% icon "far:calendar" %}
	{%- when "jam" %}{% icon "fas:headphones" %}
	{%- when "repost" %}{% icon "fas:retweet" %}
	{%- when "rsvp" %}{% icon "far:calendar-check" %}
	{%- else %}{% icon "far:comment" %}
{%- endcase -%}
